#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134340 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc8d4944-9005-5712-ad88-744dac83603e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Point of Intersection of a Circle and a Radial Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd96ba1-2b4a-52b0-ae56-d48afc1ad438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4\\sqrt{3},4\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324095} {:answer/id #uuid "2ed05277-6e18-5e15-8940-2ac1cc7e711a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4\\sqrt{3},4\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324343} {:answer/id #uuid "45a4f7ba-02b2-575e-9878-19dffb79d143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,4\\sqrt{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324534} {:answer/id #uuid "5ba9dd42-5731-5299-842c-9b4b8a43aecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,4\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324727} {:answer/id #uuid "eedf37c4-e836-577f-8644-c79747d63f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4\\sqrt{3},4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eedf37c4-e836-577f-8644-c79747d63f14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4\\sqrt{3},4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326080} :answer-field/id #uuid "c09b660e-acc3-5ec3-9d23-f8cb222700d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326568}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7c864f9-8a06-59dd-91e8-789300497ddc" :question/math-academy-id "q-41263" :question/problem "![](images/34/34b473c8e212297d8cb434fe0a2dd9872cfa2fda924ac3a4d528bc1318af8c5f.png)\n\nThe polar curve $r=8$ and the ray $\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ intersect at the point $P,$ as shown above. What are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The polar coordinates of $P$ are $(r,\\theta )=(8,\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$ We can convert the polar coordinates of $P$ to Cartesian coordinates, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{3} \\\\ y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-4\\sqrt{3},4).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068753 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8058df30-04de-555c-adfa-61fbf2b0ff31" :knowledge-point/title "Adding Rational Expressions in One Variable With Common Factors in the Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15017b89-6a83-59c3-8ca4-1e65d3e32c85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{45}{1-2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324161} {:answer/id #uuid "3a903b7b-dcca-5c4f-8920-9a1546e6dcf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-14y+45}{5(1-2y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324443} {:answer/id #uuid "c79526ea-db45-5cfa-a2b6-882255022a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14y}{5(1-2y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325697} {:answer/id #uuid "dc042986-d3e3-5167-8273-d4f156249300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{26y-45}{5(1-2y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325890} {:answer/id #uuid "e379b819-7fe0-521e-bbc1-1371d8e50ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2y+9}{1-2y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a903b7b-dcca-5c4f-8920-9a1546e6dcf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{-14y+45}{5(1-2y)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324443} :answer-field/id #uuid "36e51594-6076-558b-b4c1-486d8c2bf0d5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e010d20d-afd2-59fa-8a1c-50d451ce4776" :question/math-academy-id "q-41576" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{6y}{5(1-2y)}=p$ and $\\frac{9-4y}{1-2y}=q,$ what is $p+q?$" :question/worked-solution "We wish to add the following fractions:\n\n$$\np+q=\\frac{6y}{5(1-2y)}+\\frac{9-4y}{1-2y}\n$$\n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $5(1-2y)$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y}{5(1-2y)}+\\frac{9-4y}{1-2y} & = \\\\ \\frac{6y}{5(1-2y)}+\\frac{5}{5}\\cdot \\frac{9-4y}{1-2y} & = \\\\ \\frac{6y}{5(1-2y)}+\\frac{5(9-4y)}{5(1-2y)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6y+5(9-4y)}{5(1-2y)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6y+45-20y}{5(1-2y)} & = \\\\ \\frac{-14y+45}{5(1-2y)} & \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129124 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5696c2d5-4e35-5ed3-a4a2-6fe9b158e461" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Transformed Sinusoidal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d1c4191-fab1-56ef-9a9e-5df4f5a37573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [4,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324871} {:answer/id #uuid "705447cb-ac85-5790-aadf-544a4a2ca55d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [-2,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324896} {:answer/id #uuid "c37b50d3-93b0-5e4b-a2f6-ad5ca8b620b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [3,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325652} {:answer/id #uuid "d9fbb5f9-1876-576d-956d-164f993762da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [2,4]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325870} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d1017a-3133-56bf-ad84-e9bd0f77a8d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [2,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325976}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3d1017a-3133-56bf-ad84-e9bd0f77a8d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\in [2,6]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325976} :answer-field/id #uuid "5600e685-5275-5ef3-a75f-13f121192c83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8be6063d-ee1d-5aea-9fe3-f1f6572dff56" :question/math-academy-id "q-41840" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $y=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})+4?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-2$ and then adding $4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})\\le 1 \\\\ 2 & \\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})\\ge -2 \\\\ 6 & \\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{30}^{∘})+4\\ge 2 \\\\ 2 & \\le y\\le 6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [2,6].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101407 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100876 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89362140-1a17-56fd-a9ab-4da336112bee" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Matrix by a Column or Row of the Identity Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a95370d-414b-5eac-8919-246de33eac09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099604} {:answer/id #uuid "a84bcb4e-521f-5ea1-9075-3e249dbed932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3.5 \\\\ -2.5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099605} {:answer/id #uuid "e006e13f-10ad-5b98-98da-0e4073b443c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099606} {:answer/id #uuid "2c32ad2d-131b-5f58-b76f-c00ad96820b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099607} {:answer/id #uuid "695edc9d-dd29-5f2a-b8fd-06ab5abd1f2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099608}] :answer-field/id #uuid "954dd7be-0875-59ee-8cb2-ab4ad7d267c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e77b0e35-b8ea-5618-ab6c-8503315df0e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3.5 \\\\ -2.5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392443} {:answer/id #uuid "b90bbe8b-d8e5-5080-9aa2-4142743a4b96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392444} {:answer/id #uuid "6b52aa96-4f70-58ea-b2cf-28f779b7b43b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392445} {:answer/id #uuid "d06d67b6-8acb-58a8-957c-d55d012736a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392446} {:answer/id #uuid "e47cb90f-8189-59b3-96b0-469513eb54fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b90bbe8b-d8e5-5080-9aa2-4142743a4b96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392444} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cb1f592-094a-5b91-bac8-80971fe96ac3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bde0cdd0-7dbe-5ba4-9b36-e66cfe099501" :question/math-academy-id "q-41949" :question/problem "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5 \\\\ -2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ is the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $1$st *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $1$st *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} & -3 & 3.5 \\\\ -2 & 2\\sqrt{5} & -2.5 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7}\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+3.5\\cdot 0 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1+2\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 0+(-2.5)\\cdot 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{7} \\\\ -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "05669abb-838d-5b1c-b97f-833a28b1d413" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Points in the Case of One or No Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ffa3959-bcae-53d4-b750-3acd046f4817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067175} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f13b0a-3767-5aac-9371-497ed9cc05f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067176} {:answer/id #uuid "15c4250c-ec22-5c0f-9869-16bf0a21f119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067177} {:answer/id #uuid "76e00e67-6b8c-5712-9e4a-778c86b82f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined because the curve and the line do not intersect." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067178} {:answer/id #uuid "7c894e31-8bab-5c7b-bdc4-511f737f9090" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067179}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f5ce676b-13f0-56a5-846b-a845f49e5220" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "962a836e-7e7f-5b74-b466-74f9bd961b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined because the curve and the line do not intersect." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402751} {:answer/id #uuid "77e775d2-5c5f-53ca-8556-acf6dc6fb1d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402752} {:answer/id #uuid "a16d7da4-393e-5805-87b6-3a9b82bafe2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402753} {:answer/id #uuid "123f0263-f92c-574c-8223-205921ca12c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402754} {:answer/id #uuid "5842cb4f-dfe1-5bcd-a5d1-aca7e442c719" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "962a836e-7e7f-5b74-b466-74f9bd961b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined because the curve and the line do not intersect." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402751} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d28ac66-acba-540c-ab94-2ffd038f2893" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402750}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "801b9317-386e-554f-9207-4d232469922d" :question/math-academy-id "q-41957" :question/problem "If the line $y=-2x+3$ and the curve $y=\\frac{2}{x-2}+1$ intersect at the point $(p,q),$ then $p+q=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=-2x+3 &  \\\\ y=\\frac{2}{x-2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the equations equal to one another and solving, we get a quadratic equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+3 & =\\frac{2}{x-2}+1 \\\\ -2x+2 & =\\frac{2}{x-2} \\\\ (-2x+2)(x-2) & =2 \\\\ 2(-x+1)(x-2) & =2 \\\\ (-x+1)(x-2) & =1 \\\\ -{x}^{2}+3x-2 & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}-3x+3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-3\\pm \\sqrt{{3}^{2}-4(1)(3)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\pm \\sqrt{9-12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\pm \\sqrt{-3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root of a negative number is not a real number, so there are no real solutions. Consequently, the line $y=-2x+3$ does not intersect the hyperbola $y=\\frac{2}{x-2}+1.$\n\nA sketch of the situation is shown below.\n\n![](images/41/41fee04552a47d93f1dbd788e69e12c4b58e377ec4c0b63c3ed55c712d337f94.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392448 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc44afbe-5d76-5e09-9981-f46801ba7f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392450} {:answer/id #uuid "52743f64-5575-5f50-ab83-057fdf07b94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392451} {:answer/id #uuid "56be43e4-cbda-5ce6-b53d-23acb1dfe969" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392452} {:answer/id #uuid "77068922-3e71-5bec-a56b-febc23200124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392453} {:answer/id #uuid "55501deb-48c2-5461-b4b5-3c1803f7a5f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc44afbe-5d76-5e09-9981-f46801ba7f6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392450} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb19f32f-0991-5b71-b98c-bdea9bdda5e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54c6b58b-7b12-5b44-8e47-3a85c2ee0cea" :question/math-academy-id "q-41981" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $4$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129772 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129115 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe0050b2-b5bc-54a6-aeaf-94cd5d7e5dfb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Operations That Would Transform a Matrix To Row Echelon Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "235dc5af-aefe-5bea-8651-43b78d1c968f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{21}$ and ${a}_{43}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324261} {:answer/id #uuid "2e25d52d-b3a1-56c2-a229-c83120279d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{21}$,  ${a}_{33}$, and ${a}_{44}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324339} {:answer/id #uuid "7abca97a-1851-5e67-9633-f11bcb2e2e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{22}$ and ${a}_{33}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324999} {:answer/id #uuid "982046e6-3f52-5bfb-bc6b-db4bf8c78d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{21}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325263} {:answer/id #uuid "e435a192-10d9-5156-8113-e7659f0e7728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{43}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "235dc5af-aefe-5bea-8651-43b78d1c968f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${a}_{21}$ and ${a}_{43}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324261} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6cca789-922a-5bd0-8ef3-f5775a87662b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ab2c24d-7d61-5976-acd1-acab7ad4094a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42008" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{21}$ and ${a}_{43}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟶\\,[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115241 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d81e3f1-d930-59ee-b439-2a3645aebb6c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Consistent System of Equations Using Gauss-Jordan Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e80e6ba-d53c-56a1-8f14-814656e252d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402758} {:answer/id #uuid "240d49db-221f-5c96-a2c7-752016dd8d06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1-z \\\\ 0 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402759} {:answer/id #uuid "c205ae90-dae6-5981-8476-c566174adf7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-z \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402760} {:answer/id #uuid "a7eb10d8-4da4-5dab-bc8c-4a003f7cebfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402761} {:answer/id #uuid "c70e171e-d942-5f58-90b7-b6fb6a232836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7eb10d8-4da4-5dab-bc8c-4a003f7cebfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402761} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fa49e40-cb09-52a9-be51-216ec3f67938" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "013e11bb-39c0-595b-a244-03847638286f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42019" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y+2z=2 \\\\  & y-z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=0 \\\\  & y-z=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=0 \\\\ y=z-1 \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ z-1 \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129082 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "98d6004a-547a-5b0b-9748-9571cc3ee632" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Tangent or Cotangent Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c61dc7c0-d3f8-5a52-a767-d5a5950ed61b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan θ =-4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128132} {:answer/id #uuid "3c3acfbd-450b-529e-9e81-f6898d0afc15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan θ =-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128133} {:answer/id #uuid "425120b8-9a7a-509b-b2b1-16f549aee0d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan θ = \\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128134} {:answer/id #uuid "51495d9a-03f0-5f49-aeab-3c6ea5811fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan θ =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128135} {:answer/id #uuid "681b517b-c0da-555d-9464-011b10f62e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\tan θ = \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128136}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a1f2f1dc-9d19-53e5-af38-cc9ea5f6ad94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128131} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2ab46d8-4b20-5cb0-bd03-d4843745957e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "tan⁡\\theta =-4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402771} {:answer/id #uuid "1281daa1-21d2-521b-ba7b-2f63be883923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "tan⁡\\theta =\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402772} {:answer/id #uuid "cf49d4c9-aad2-5d7f-bca3-cd2582a8d854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "tan⁡\\theta =\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402773} {:answer/id #uuid "1efc176a-2f08-5690-b21d-dbaa2aa9e6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "tan⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402774} {:answer/id #uuid "9257c9b4-8a20-5a75-b76e-4b9c11a339a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "tan⁡\\theta =-\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1efc176a-2f08-5690-b21d-dbaa2aa9e6f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "tan⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402774} :answer-field/id #uuid "737f5b1b-3e66-5582-9362-63911dfedfe9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "299c91a4-6289-5d24-ace1-495b52634a62" :question/math-academy-id "q-42043" :question/problem "![](images/91/919b9e8f2a9493fd0dda3e0d7bf66de9af054fc4ed9c0fcf7a68329fdbbaffdd.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the unit circle. Given that $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2},$ what is the value of $tan⁡\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/94/948610f67267e6ec1b845d2b4e1bc4030b81a1080bcb9a44d9f974ff78c3f7b0.png)\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $cos⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe select the negative answer since $cos⁡\\theta $ is negative in the second quadrant. So, $cos⁡\\theta =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$\n\nFinally, knowing that $tan⁡\\theta =\\frac{sin⁡\\theta }{cos⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡\\theta =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119772 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c348ec0d-ec14-5ab3-b31b-62c45b43c86b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118641} {:answer/id #uuid "f799ec7b-3561-5729-a81c-88e3d3e97416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118642} {:answer/id #uuid "2953424a-c761-5832-bf1c-5ad1e817b628" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118643} {:answer/id #uuid "6838e181-7f7b-53d2-beaa-db8004fec2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118644} {:answer/id #uuid "7d7c341f-ecc1-5d20-bddd-1103016b4f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118645}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9c79ad-5239-5ddd-bf74-1e3f8db763bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118640} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0babb588-cb94-586c-9b9b-239ddf850608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402777} {:answer/id #uuid "56b0c175-3bca-5e71-b0bd-6ea1ec15fb38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402778} {:answer/id #uuid "97735f63-e217-562f-8ab3-d21dfe4643a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402779} {:answer/id #uuid "188af51f-738d-54fb-a2fd-9eb0c1f48912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402780} {:answer/id #uuid "341ee6bc-c870-5be4-a9af-153355b7a5a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0babb588-cb94-586c-9b9b-239ddf850608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402777} :answer-field/id #uuid "eba24bc4-353b-563d-b970-3c4e99c8ae95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a1fe1df-e314-527e-a884-f0c092b97472" :question/math-academy-id "q-42090" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 11\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{31} & =5\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =3\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119773 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1637e23-6566-5e45-af4c-b27333f882d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Row"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2645148c-8f0c-59d8-8328-daf1c11c002e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324280} {:answer/id #uuid "8423c962-04ae-56a6-a351-28d4870327a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325084} {:answer/id #uuid "8cbab88f-65b0-53c1-8212-e69a999b2288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325165} {:answer/id #uuid "8ed70273-c8e9-55fc-8960-e486a7629dcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325182} {:answer/id #uuid "d57a2363-d584-51bb-988e-accd88178c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2645148c-8f0c-59d8-8328-daf1c11c002e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324280} :answer-field/id #uuid "60a39b12-5834-56dc-bd92-b12e1a44915e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "00bb680c-6e72-5c8f-931f-0ff9d17c1cfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-42095" :question/problem "Calculate\n$|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|.$" :question/worked-solution "The $3$rd row of the matrix contains two zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{33}+1\\cdot {C}_{34} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{3+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $3$rd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{31}+2\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{33} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1-2)-2(2-4) \\\\  & =-1+4 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+(-4)\\cdot {C}_{22}+(-2)\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4(2+3)+2(1+6) \\\\  & =-20+14 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|=2\\cdot 3-(-6)=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119774 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Column"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc5eb029-0132-5889-8fc5-5f965ee2f59e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392470} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc017a6-b39b-5798-8cb8-8c48adc144d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392471} {:answer/id #uuid "7716a567-64dd-5858-bbd8-e8ca9e8cb026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392472} {:answer/id #uuid "132feae2-50ab-5b05-8f53-cad56d65c01d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392473} {:answer/id #uuid "4e655a97-1883-5c02-9bf7-e53331009763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7716a567-64dd-5858-bbd8-e8ca9e8cb026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392472} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e783258-40f2-5eea-94b3-4ec1ceb99f44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9e1a0ecf-c99d-5b41-851f-c3bc683d9006" :question/math-academy-id "q-42104" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "Using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{14}+2\\cdot {C}_{24}+0\\cdot {C}_{34}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119773 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1637e23-6566-5e45-af4c-b27333f882d1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using a Laplace Expansion Across a Row"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6067ab7f-666f-51fe-a3ad-de2b5d607d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370935} {:answer/id #uuid "c031e32c-214f-5b2c-8394-eab613b8d9d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370936} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe9381e-b0ef-5210-b4ea-f2615e9433da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370937} {:answer/id #uuid "7d661da1-7cdc-5100-b6d8-e9dfbca11fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370938} {:answer/id #uuid "e88af25c-0464-5342-b56b-d091bcd4dd1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e88af25c-0464-5342-b56b-d091bcd4dd1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370939} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e5bc926-a168-5bf8-9c60-65f432035bc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe1a4bd6-0ca7-5877-a7c4-a06ff6754131" :question/math-academy-id "q-42106" :question/problem "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $3$rd row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using cofactor expansion along the third row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{31}+2\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{33}+0\\cdot {C}_{34} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=-2\\cdot 6=-12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110568 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "69d6ed5b-1c29-53a7-a37e-817042a02861" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing the Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85251810-38ab-5c23-8000-832183eefbba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e9/e97a7603936b6e125189e9868df34291e145aac878ca64c1c03761bf544fbbec.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186108728} {:answer/id #uuid "abdfb5b0-c85f-5799-b427-6af8ee1ed617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/326290611c8ca441f0d9bcc0439678f0c29302b2784ee4fe65e69a3008ec8fe3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 1759